{{ pageHeader("Mobile Car Window & Back Glass Replacement", "Broken door window, shattered back glass, or a cracked side mirror? Fresh Start Auto Glass replaces it at your home or work anywhere in north DFW, and cleans up the broken glass so your vehicle is secure and ready to drive.") }}

<div class="wrap rows">
  <section class="row" id="door-glass" aria-labelledby="door-title">
    <h2 id="door-title">Door and side window replacement</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Door glass is tempered, so when it breaks it shatters into hundreds of small pieces. Most of them end up inside the door panel, in the window track, and all over the seats and floor.</p>
      <p>We remove the door panel, clear the broken glass out of the door and the track, install the new window, and check that it rolls up and down smoothly and seals properly. Then we vacuum the interior so you're not finding glass for weeks.</p>
      <p>We also replace the small fixed side windows, often called quarter glass or vent glass, on most vehicles.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" id="back-glass" aria-labelledby="back-title">
    <h2 id="back-title">Back glass (rear windshield) replacement</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Back glass usually breaks all at once and often takes the defroster lines with it. Many rear windows also carry the radio antenna or wiring for a rear wiper or brake light.</p>
      <p>We install new back glass with the right seal, reconnect the defroster, antenna, and wiring connections where your vehicle has them, and vacuum the cargo area and back seat. That includes SUV liftgate glass and rear truck windows.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" id="mirror-glass" aria-labelledby="mirror-title">
    <h2 id="mirror-title">Side mirror glass replacement</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>A cracked or missing side mirror is a blind spot. If the mirror housing is fine and only the glass is damaged, we can usually replace just the glass, including heated and convex mirror glass on many models. That costs far less than a whole new mirror assembly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row row-dark" aria-labelledby="breakin-title">
    <h2 id="breakin-title">After a break-in: what to do</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Stay safe and call the police</strong> if anything was stolen. Get a report number if you need one.</li>
        <li><strong>Take photos</strong> of the damage before anything is cleaned up.</li>
        <li><strong>Cover the opening</strong> with plastic and tape to keep rain out, and avoid driving with an open window if you can.</li>
        <li><strong>Call us.</strong> We'll come to you, replace the glass, and clean up the mess, usually the same day or next day.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-light" href="/contact/#quote">Get a free quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="quote-title">
    <h2 id="quote-title">What we need for a quote</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Tell us your year, make, and model, which window is broken, and where you are. The VIN helps, since the same model can use different glass. A photo of the damage is useful too. See every service we offer on our <a href="/services/">Services page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

